# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Succession from the superseded predecessor is FORCED, landed 2026-08-03.
#
# User directive (conversion-taxonomy.md § SUCCESSION): "It should not be opt in.
# it should be a forced succession... that interaction has to provide dependable
# outcomes, otherwise it will be impossible to measure success and make patches."
#
# The argument is measurement, not convenience: an opt-in marker gives one command
# on one tree two possible outcomes depending on whether someone remembered a line,
# so two runs cannot be compared and no patch can be shown to have helped.
#
# The SAFETY is that it is forced from ONE named predecessor. Workforce supersedes
# claude-enforcer and nothing else; any other generator keeps every refusal
# (fixture f2-two-generators).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
