# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data-in-hand, landed 2026-08-03 — clause 2f.
#
# Clause 2 closed only half the user's directive. Its predicate is a Mechanicals
# row with Scope: derived, and all five of its refusals resolve to a spawn — so
# the commonest cheap answer of all, "the data is already here", was on no rung
# at any point. A roster question answered from a chart already loaded is not a
# command and can never become a row in that table.
#
# The asymmetry INVERTS relative to clause 2, which is why 2g is stricter than
# 2b: a wrong mechanical dispatch returns a wrong answer with an exit code to
# catch it; a wrong direct answer returns a confident one with nothing behind it.
# Hence 2h — the artifact is cited or the clause did not fire.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

