# ── The three weak points the design shipped with, closed 2026-07-31 ──────────
# 1. Coverage is matched by reading a prose cell. A positive claim reads
#    charitably; a stated BOUNDARY does not, and an unclear match resolves to an
#    agent rather than to a cheap wrong answer.
# 2. A row had no negative test while maintainers now do. `Proven` inherits one
#    where it exists and says `unproven` where it does not — which dispatches, but
#    never as a bare PASS.
# 3. Two rows claiming the same work was left to a dispatch-time tiebreak. It is a
#    defect in the TABLE; the door refuses, `index` reports.
check(
    "org: an unclear coverage match resolves to an agent, not to a guess",
    "unsure is not whole" in _org_block
    and "Being wrong toward an agent costs one hop" in _org_block,
    "clause 2a must say what happens when totality is UNCLEAR — without it a literal "
    "reader treats plausible-but-unconfirmed as total, which is the whole risk",
)
